# Awwwards UI

Before designing, building, or modifying any UI component or page, call the `awwwards-design-agent` MCP tools and wait for their results:

1. `audit_project_design` — pass the project root (or its `package.json`) and install any packages it reports as missing before writing UI.
2. `get_awwwards_blueprint` — pick the vibe that fits the surface (`dark-luxury-tech`, `editorial-swiss`, or `clean-neo-minimal`) and apply its tokens, type, borders, lighting, and motion.
3. `get_high_craft_component` — when the work is a bento grid, editorial hero, or floating glass nav, request that `componentType` and follow the returned architecture.

Do not start layout, styling, or component code until those calls have returned. Use the tool output as the design source for structure, motion, and visual tokens.

Published sentences still come from `content/legacy-site.md`.
